          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_caption",
              "index": 1,
              "bbox": [
                0.106,
                0.098,
                0.627,
                0.115
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Table 1. Comparison of photovoltaic technologies (approximate values) "
                },
                {
                  "type": "equation_inline",
                  "content": "{}^{1}"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 2,
              "bbox": [
                0.1,
                0.12,
                0.905,
                0.304
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_1_table_2.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">Group</td><td rowspan=\"2\">Technology</td><td colspan=\"2\">Absorber</td><td rowspan=\"2\">Typical module efficiency, %</td><td rowspan=\"2\">Market status</td></tr><tr><td>Band gap, eV</td><td>Band gap type</td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">Crystalline silicon</td><td>Monocrystalline Si</td><td>1.12</td><td>indirect</td><td>20 – 23</td><td>dominant</td></tr><tr><td>Multicrystalline Si</td><td>1.12</td><td>indirect</td><td>16 – 18</td><td>declining</td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"3\">Thin film</td><td>CdTe</td><td>1.45</td><td>direct</td><td>18 – 19</td><td>utility scale</td></tr><tr><td>CIGS</td><td>1.0 – 1.7</td><td>direct</td><td>14 – 17</td><td>niche</td></tr><tr><td>Amorphous Si</td><td>1.7</td><td>amorphous</td><td>6 – 9</td><td>legacy</td></tr><tr><td>Emerging</td><td>Perovskite</td><td>1.5 – 1.6</td><td>direct</td><td>—</td><td>early commercial</td></tr></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.103,
            0.325,
            0.298,
            0.344
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Worked example"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.102,
            0.357,
            0.531,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A monocrystalline cell of  "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "156 \\times 156"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "  mm under STC has:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.38,
            0.349,
            0.401
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1 "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "V_{\\mathrm{oc}} = 0.67\\mathrm{V}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "I_{\\mathrm{sc}} = 9.5\\mathrm{A}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ";"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.404,
            0.564,
            0.425
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2 fill factor "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "FF = 0.80"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", so "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "P_{\\max} = 0.80 \\times 0.67 \\times 9.5 \\approx 5.1 \\mathrm{~W}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ";"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.428,
            0.552,
            0.448
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3 incident power  "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "P_{in} = 1000 \\, W/m^{2} \\times 0.0243 \\, m^{2} \\approx 24.3 \\, W"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ;"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.454,
            0.368,
            0.47
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4 efficiency "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\eta \\approx 5.1 / 24.3\\approx 21\\%"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.101,
            0.484,
            0.248,
            0.502
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Conclusions"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.094,
            0.515,
            0.772,
            0.534
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Crystalline silicon dominates the market thanks to mature manufacturing and low cost."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.093,
            0.54,
            0.742,
            0.558
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "- Efficiency is limited by the band gap: the Shockley–Queisser limit is about 33.7%."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.092,
            0.564,
            0.702,
            0.582
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Tandem cells, e.g. perovskite on silicon, can exceed the single-junction limit."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.102,
            0.597,
            0.691,
            0.616
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "^{1}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "  Efficiency figures are typical values for commercial products and vary between manufacturers."
            }
          ]
        }
